      "text": "                                                                       GREENKO INTEGRATED MANAGEMENT SYSTEM\n\n                                                                    WORK INSTRUCTION FOR LEAKAGE IN THE HUB\n\n    1.   PURPOSE\n\n         This document describes the standard operating procedure for Leakage in the HUB\n\n    2.   SCOPE\n\n         This document applies to Gamesa model in G97 & G114.\n\n    3.   RESPONSIBILITY\n\n         Authorised person only\n\n    4.   SPARES, CONSUMABLES, TOOLS & TACKLES.\n         Tools:   1. Multimeter - 1 No,\n                  2. Spanner set - 1 set,\n                  3. Screw driver & Voltage tester - 1 No each,\n                  4. Craft work box (small) - 1 No.\n         Spares & Consumables:\n              1. Hub leak sensor.\n              2. Hub leak sensor Cable.\n    5.   DOCUMENTS & RECORDS\n\n        Title                                                  Form No.\n     Work permit\n\n   Work at height       F-CO-EHS-13-08\n\nElectrical isolation    F-CO-EHS-13-04\n\n     Check list       CL- Wind-SG-EM-211\n\n    6.   Safety Requirements:\n        1.    Basic PPE's - Safety Shoe, Safety Helmet, Hand Gloves, safety harness etc.\n        2.    Read turbine safety manual before carrying out any work in the turbine\n        3.    Always complete safety documentation part - work permit etc.\n        4.    Risk assessments and HIRA to be cross checked for the Job activity.\n        5.    690 V/ 230 V will be available on control panel. Be careful.\n    7.   ERROR CRITERIA\n\n         This alarm is trigger when More than 3 seconds without detecting the sensor signal of leaks in the\n         HUB.\n\n    8.   PROCEDURE\n            1    Check for any Physical Oil leakage in hub.\n            2    Check the Hub leak sensor.\n            3    Check the hub leak contactor connections.\n            4    Check the DI module for any malfunction.\n            5    Replace the failure component.\n\n\n\n\n\n    WI-WIND-SG-EM-212    I1. R0/01.07.2019                     Page 1 of 1\n                      INTERNAL",
